caption: Overview
tradition-component: overview

Shadow Arts uses one fixed institutional Jutsu tree. The practitioner learns authored techniques rather than improvising effects, develops through the tree's prerequisites and Potence gates, and eventually masters one sufficiently deep body of forms. Shadow Arts Potence is the character's Kung Fu Higher Purpose. Practicum turns sustained Jutsu use into additional training toward descendant techniques; Blood of the Dragon permits two different Jutsu selections in one action cycle without granting additional actions; Hundred Schools permits simultaneous study across multiple Jutsu lineages and, after sufficient initiation into a tree, self-directed completion of its pre-Mastery curriculum.
